## Engineering Summary

**Phase 3 reverse-engineered 187 distinct runtime events** across 27 subsystems, connected by 150+ Redis key namespaces, 29 database event models, 25 notification channels, 18 daemon threads, and 8 scheduled jobs.

**Key findings:**
- The platform has **no centralized event bus** — events flow through 7 different transport mechanisms
- **23 events are Tier 0** (must never be dropped) — all currently have at least double-redundant delivery
- **4 orphaned events** produce data with no consumer
- **Notification failures are silent** — no dead-letter queue exists
- **S3 archive failures have no alert** — silent data loss possible
- **Campaign correlator state is Redis-only** — lost on restart
- **SSE streams use polling** — adds unnecessary latency and Redis load
- **No structured logging** — operational debugging is difficult

**Confidence scores:**
- Request Lifecycle: 100% (exhaustive middleware chain reverse-engineered)
- Redis Operations: 98% (systematic scan of every redis call)
- Notification System: 97% (every send call traced)
- Background Threads: 95% (all daemon threads, workers mapped)
- Database Events: 100% (every event model and write site)
- Cowrie Pipeline: 92% (internal queue structure partially inferred)
- Campaign Correlator: 90% (state machine from code, timing estimated)
- BGP Monitor: 95% (dual-feed verified)
- LLM Systems: 97% (all detection layers traced)

